TASK 4 – SMART MANUFACTURING OPTIMISATION
Dynamic Programming for Assembly Line Scheduling (7 Marks)
Programming Language: Python
Algorithm: Dynamic Programming
Objective: Find the minimum production time and the optimal sequence of stations across two assembly lines.
1. Problem Analysis
A manufacturing company operates two parallel assembly lines. Each line contains the same number of processing stations.

A product can:
1. Continue on the same assembly line.
2. Transfer to the other assembly line before entering the next station.
Each station has a processing time. Transferring between lines also requires additional time.

The objective is to calculate the minimum total production time and identify the optimal route.
Input Dataset
We consider two assembly lines with four stations each.
Parameter	Line 1	Line 2
Station 1	4	5
Station 2	5	6
Station 3	3	5
Station 4	2	4

Transfer times:
Transfer	Time
Line 1 to Line 2	7, 4, 5
Line 2 to Line 1	2, 3, 2

Entry times:
- Line 1 = 2
- Line 2 = 3
Exit times:
- Line 1 = 3
- Line 2 = 2
2. Dynamic Programming Approach
Let:
- f1[j] = Minimum time to reach station j on Line 1.
- f2[j] = Minimum time to reach station j on Line 2.
- a1[j] = Processing time on Line 1.
- a2[j] = Processing time on Line 2.
- t1[j] = Transfer time from Line 1 to Line 2.
- t2[j] = Transfer time from Line 2 to Line 1.
Initial conditions:
\[
f_1[1]=e_1+a_1[1]
\]

\[
f_2[1]=e_2+a_2[1]
\]

Transition equations:
\[
f_1[j]=\min
\begin{cases}
f_1[j-1]+a_1[j]\\
f_2[j-1]+t_2[j-1]+a_1[j]
\end{cases}
\]

\[
f_2[j]=\min
\begin{cases}
f_2[j-1]+a_2[j]\\
f_1[j-1]+t_1[j-1]+a_2[j]
\end{cases}
\]

Final minimum time:
\[
T=\min(f_1[n]+x_1,\ f_2[n]+x_2)
\]


3. Task 4.1 – Build the Optimisation Engine (3 Marks)
Python Source Code
The following program calculates minimum production time, displays stay-versus-transfer decisions, and reconstructs the optimal route.
# ASSEMBLY LINE SCHEDULING USING DPdef assembly_line(a1, a2, t1, t2, e1, e2, x1, x2):    n = len(a1)    f1 = [0] * n    f2 = [0] * n    # Store previous line for route reconstruction    p1 = [0] * n    p2 = [0] * n    # Entry time and first station    f1[0] = e1 + a1[0]    f2[0] = e2 + a2[0]    print("INITIAL DP VALUES")    print("Line 1:", f1[0])    print("Line 2:", f2[0])    print("\nDP DECISION TABLE")    print("Station | L1 Stay | L1 Transfer | Selected")    print("        | L2 Stay | L2 Transfer | Selected")    # Calculate DP values    for j in range(1, n):        # Line 1 decisions        stay1 = f1[j - 1] + a1[j]        transfer1 = f2[j - 1] + t2[j - 1] + a1[j]        if stay1 <= transfer1:            f1[j] = stay1



