5. Final Result
The Assembly Line Scheduling problem was successfully implemented using Dynamic Programming in Python.
The experiments demonstrated:
1. The minimum production time for the normal case is 19.
2. The program displays stay and transfer decisions at every station.
3. Increasing the transfer time did not change the optimal route.
4. Increasing the processing time at Station 2 caused the optimal route to change.
5. The new minimum production time became 25.
6. The extension to three assembly lines requires additional DP states, transitions and predecessor information.
Conclusion: Dynamic Programming helps manufacturing companies minimize production time by selecting the most efficient assembly-line route. It can also adapt to changing transfer costs and machine disruptions by recalculating the optimal route.
